      revoke credentials that you have found exposed on GitHub or elsewhere.\nL16: ## cite5†Revoke
      a list of credentials L17: \nL18: Submit a list of credentials to be revoked. This endpoint
      is intended to revoke credentials the caller does not own and may have found exposed on
      GitHub.com or elsewhere. It can also be used for credentials associated with an old user
      account that you no longer have access to. Credential owners will be notified of the
      revocation.\nL19: \nL20: This endpoint currently accepts the following credential types:\nL21:
      * Personal access tokens (classic) (`ghp_`)\nL22: * Fine-grained personal access tokens
      (`github_pat_`)\nL23: * OAuth app access tokens (`gho_`)\nL24: * User-to-server tokens from
      GitHub Apps (`ghu_`)\nL25: * Refresh tokens from GitHub Apps (`ghr_`)\nL26: \nL27: Revoked
      credentials may impact users on GitHub Free, Pro, & Team and GitHub Enterprise Cloud, and
      GitHub Enterprise Cloud with Enterprise Managed Users. GitHub cannot reactivate any
      credentials that have been revoked; new credentials will need to be generated.\nL28: To
      prevent abuse, this API is limited to only 60 unauthenticated requests per hour and a max of
      1000 tokens per API request.\nL29: \nL30: Note\nL31: \nL32: Any authenticated requests will
      return a 403.\nL33: ### cite6†Parameters for \"Revoke a list of credentials\" L34: \nL35:
      Headers\nL36: `accept` string Setting to `application/vnd.github+json` is recommended.\nL37:
      Body parameters\nL38: `credentials` array of strings Required A list of credentials to be
      revoked, up to 1000 per request.\nL39: \nL40: ### cite7†HTTP response status codes for
      \"Revoke a list of credentials\" L41: \nL42: Status code | Description\nL43: --- | ---\nL44:
      `202` | Accepted\nL45: `422` | Validation failed, or the endpoint has been spammed.\nL46:
      `500` | Internal Error\nL47: ### cite8†Code samples for \"Revoke a list of credentials\"
      L48: #### Request example\nL49: \nL50: post/credentials/revoke\nL51: \nL52: * cURL\nL53:
      \nL54: * JavaScript\nL55: \nL56: * GitHub CLI\nL57: \nL58: Copy to clipboard curl request
